    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** stands as the definitive anchor of the lineup with an elite 82.37 score. His placement in the #2 hole against Elder provides a prime opportunity for both run production and his trademark stolen base upside, which remains our primary weapon in this rotisserie race. The high score is bolstered by a favorable dynamic platoon advantage and a solid matchup against a pitcher with a 4.40 xERA. Additionally, the combo of **Max Muncy** and **Henry Bolte** represents our best value plays; both benefit from the platoon edge against Bradford, who is struggling with a 5.29 xERA. **Henry Bolte** specifically gains massive value from his leadoff spot, making him a high-leverage target to boost our counting stats.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Jose Caballero** on the bench despite his elite sprint speed profile. While he narrowly missed the cut with a 39.32 efficiency score, the combination of facing an elite arm in Cease (2.95 xERA) and his regression in platoon splits against righties forced him below our 40-point floor. Meanwhile, we continue to manage a decimated roster as **James Wood**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Vinnie Pasquantino** remain sidelined on the IL, placing additional pressure on utility pieces like **Isaac Paredes** and **Zach McKinstry** to maintain efficiency. \n\nWe are monitoring the status of **Josh Naylor** and **Cole Young**, as both are currently labeled with \"Lineup Pending\" tags. While we have projected them into the #5 and #6 spots respectively, any downward adjustment in their batting order against H. Brown could erode their marginal efficiency scores. We remain cautious regarding **Austin Riley**, whose score of 49.31 is suppressed by his current #8 spot in the order; should the lineup shift him up, he is a candidate to outperform his projection against Soroka. We are holding fast with **Gabriel Moreno** and **Mickey Moniak**, both of whom are projected for strong outings given their platoon advantages and mid-to-high order placement.",
